From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:28:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Build against upstream whatsmeow

main tracks github.com/polymorfa/hypermeow, the fork Polymorfa's
platform runs, under its own import path. purple-gowhatsapp, which
hands meowcaller its client, is built on go.mau.fi/whatsmeow, and Go
sees the two clients as different types. hypermeow was introduced as a
pure rename of the import path (0eebabe), so rename it back and pin the
whatsmeow purple-gowhatsapp uses. go mod tidy raises the go directive to
1.26 for that whatsmeow.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS: purple-gowhatsapp uses go.mau.fi/whatsmeow]
